  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nHigh and mid level clouds continue to stream across the CWA at\ntimes for Thanksgiving Day, with mainly dry and quiet weather \nexpected into tonight. An exception exists across the MT/ND border\nwith isolated rain or snow showers possible with a shortwave\ntracking east. Gusty west winds will develop with this system and\npersist into Friday. A Lake Wind Advisory issued for Fort Peck \nLake from 9 PM This evening until 5 PM Friday with wave heights as\nhigh as 5 feet at times. Look for additional gusty winds on\nSaturday.\n\nA broad lingering trough will slide into the central U.S. late\nthis weekend with ridging developing over the western CONUS. This\nwill result in continued dry but cooler weather conditions.\nHowever, as the upstream ridge flattens, the next shortwave will\ntrack from west to east with associated increased chances for\nlight rain and snow for NE Montana.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & NBM DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM led the way with the forecast period, capturing average to\nabove average confidence overall given excellent agreement among\nmodel ensemble members. Confidence decreases slightly into early\nnext week on precipitation chances given marginal thermal profiles\nand longer time scales. The only change to the forecast was for\nthe immediate term pops for collaboration purposes.",
